WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We met at a heart attack
factory, "SNL"...

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...when you hosted in 2001.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you went back recently
to play Rex Tillerson.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.842 size:81% position:41% line:92%
There you go. Sadly...

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:12.712 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was not long for
the administration, though.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
This will not be
a gravy train for you.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-He's already done.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The fine paychecks,
the fat paychecks you get

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:26.726
off being an extra on "SNL."
-When you played -- that's true.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course,
during the Lewinsky scandal,

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.263
you played Linda Tripp famously.
-Yeah.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.033
-How many times do you think you
played her over the course...

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought one too many.
But apparently they liked it.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They kept bringing you back.
-So they kept writing

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.307 size:78% position:39% line:92%
little capers for me.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just thought it was because
I looked cute in a dress.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.646
-You did.
I think everybody -- did you --

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.649 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:55.121 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there anyone
in the administration --

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.124 line:92%
now that Tillerson's out,

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
is there anyone that you
would like to play?

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I want to be
the thug that threatened

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stormy Daniels
in the parking lot.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.133 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I want to be that guy.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.868 size:78% position:39%
There's a lot of ways
you can go with that.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:09.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can get like
the Rudy Giuliani thing,

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is like a second-rate
Tom Hagen.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.409 line:92%
-Yeah, well, that's the thing.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because of what we're seeing
as far as the aptitude

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
of everybody
in this administration,

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
he might not have been
an effective thug.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:26.019
Like, he might have been,
like, maybe less thuggish

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
than a normal guy.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.688 size:81% position:41%
-He might have gone up
to her and been like,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Excuse me,
are you Stormy Daniels?"

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:34.527 size:88% position:44%
-"Before you sign this,
could you do me a favor,

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.696 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
just lay off Trump?

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.231 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I love your work."

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.732 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:43.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The last time you hosted
that I was there,

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wrote a sketch,
and you were so wonderful.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
It did not go to air.
-No.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a hard cut
between dress and air.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It was a scene where you

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.247 line:92%
worked at a novelty toy factory.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:55.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You were the boss.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there you are.
-You know why the bit died?

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why?
-That mustache.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you think?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.490 line:92%
-It was a killer mustache.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.826 size:84% position:42%
And the thing was there
were breakaway chairs.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it was
a novelty toy store,

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
so all the chairs
were breakaway.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:11.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And Bobby Moynihan

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.800
was your employee, and you
kept giving him bad news.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
And every time he sat down,
the chair would break.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.370 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"No, try this one."
No, this is good.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.641
-Do you remember Ken Aymong,
who is the producer there?

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, Kenny.
-So, Kenny,

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember when we did it.
He -- Kenny's the guy

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:25.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's in charge
of the budget each week.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes, "Pally,
this sketch better work,

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
because these chairs
cost a fortune."

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:30.683 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:34.454
-Did he use the term "Pally?"
-He did use the term "Pally."

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:37.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is a catchphrase
of Ken Aymong.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.626
But you gave it your all.
I take full responsibility.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:42.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought it was a great bit.
The audience, not so much.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.396 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, and it was --

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:46.366
-I think they were taking
a dinner break at the time.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
-And you've hosted enough

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
to know that wasn't like
a maybe/either/or.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it was a minute into
that sketch,

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.175
I think everybody involved knew,
okay --

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's one of those sketches
if you're doing it with

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will Ferrell,
he'd step on the gas.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.715 line:92%
Not only are we going to crash,

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.018
we're going to spread this thing
over three acres.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:07.787 line:92%
-So, that used to be fun,

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, bombing in a sketch
with him.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah, 'cause it was --

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.059 size:78% position:39% line:92%
He just -- Rrrrrrrrr!

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:15.962 size:81% position:41%
-Well, that, back when
I had a desk at "SNL,"

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:19.232 size:81% position:41%
like, there was a --
you'd go on the server

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.200 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and watch old sketches.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we never watched things
that went well.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were always like,
"Did you hear the one about

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:26.372
where Will bombed so bad,
nobody in the audience

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:29.943
made a sound and he just, like,
took the longest pauses."

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like [bleep]
you ass [bleep].

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.346 line:92%
You're staying here all night.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.681 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:36.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
Always so great to see you.
-It was awesome.

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.418 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Thanks for everything.

